  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 52. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 敷地 — 建物などを設けるための土地。\n2. 識別 — 違いを見分けること。\n3. 仕切り — 空間などを区切るもの。\n4. 始業 — 授業や仕事が始まること。\n5. 仕草 — 体や手足のちょっとした動き。\n6. シグナル — 何かを知らせる合図や信号。\n7. 仕込み — 料理や仕事などの前もってする準備。\n8. 仕事場 — 仕事をする場所。\n9. 資材 — 建築や生産などに使う材料。\n10. 司書 — 図書館で本や資料の整理や案内をする専門の人。\n11. 師匠 — 芸や技などを教える先生。\n12. 試食 — 味を確かめるため少し食べてみること。\n13. 史実 — 歴史上に実際にあったとされる出来事。\n14. システム — いくつもの部分がつながって働く仕組み。\n15. 静けさ — 音や動きが少なく落ち着いている様子。\n16. 姿勢 — 立つときや座るときなどの体の形。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
